    {
      "id": "W-FILE-SIZE-PROBE",
      "type": "ux-perk",
      "title": "Learn exact movie/episode size on open with a header-only HEAD (fallback Range bytes=0-0) before playback; many IPTV providers send no size in any list/info call",
      "status": {
        "android": "MISSING",
        "winui": "HAS",
        "tv": "N-A"
      },
      "links": [
        "codex/winui-catalog-design-plan:bb0be31",
        "docs/provider-field-report.md (windows-spike)"
      ],
      "notes": "Verified on a real provider: list/info JSON has no size; the media URL answers HEAD (Content-Length) and Range 0-0 (206 + Content-Range total). Run it BEFORE playback starts, after the old stream stops, so there is never a second connection (providers often allow one). Cap ~2 s, never read a body, never probe series, never log URL. No 7-day wait for an opened item. Plausibility 1 MB-200 GB.",
      "origin": "winui"
    },
    {
      "id": "W-FILE-SIZE-ESTIMATE",
      "type": "ux-perk",
      "title": "Show \"~1.4 GB\" estimate from bitrate x duration when no exact size exists; exact replaces it",
      "status": {
        "android": "MISSING",
        "winui": "HAS",
        "tv": "N-A"
      },
      "links": [
        "codex/winui-catalog-design-plan:bb0be31"
      ],
      "notes": "estimate = total kbit/s x duration s / 8; accept 128-80,000 kbit/s, 60 s-8 h, result 1 MB-200 GB; prefer info.duration over duration_secs when they disagree; store in a separate estimated column so exact always wins; label with ~ and an approximate automation name; DB-only on cards/hover (no network on hover).",
      "origin": "winui"
    },
